{"id": "EUVD-2026-76286", "enisaUuid": "6144ef31-f45d-37aa-8827-f5e7bbebbcfb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-stats: fix a crash if allocation of per-cpu data fails\n\nIf \"dm_kvzalloc(percpu_alloc_size, cpu_to_node(cpu))\" fails, the code\njumps to the \"out\" label and calls dm_stat_free. dm_stat_free does\n\"for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) { dm_kvfree(s->stat_percpu[cpu][0].histogram,\ns->histogram_alloc_size);\", which crashes with NULL pointer dereference\nif s->stat_percpu[cpu] is NULL.\n\nThis commit fixes the bug by testing s->stat_percpu[cpu] for NULL before\nusing it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e45f0b0c41139810ff395ba2f3cfca1460a5b8a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9805d87d0e26c68ee69da3928e665214d2e2851a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/564d17573ef643c13cf6e9015124a205fa65e704", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/389a50d094e13724f5f45e6d9d6ef734c98ba291", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3f211b7a277dd404b4e7d23095be964b5b46a27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74210fa072960a18bb0eead487585452af722e4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c8f7870ed3ebd512f090d7714cc2c556b9e5c75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc87e26d9cce22061dc21e51e11afef29dbbc36a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80963", "GHSA-vfhr-8gq2-gpcv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1970e5ab-cee2-3aee-a89f-0fdb7e8ec229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "25d74b5c-683a-3e17-93d0-6af557a6bc2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "2df03fd9-f244-3e2f-9019-00298880187b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "30620d6e-37ad-3a15-90a5-ba6fcbd0ce4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}